  "worked_solution": "We summarize all the given information in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-1.5)$ | $-1.5$ | $(-1.5,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| ${f}^{″}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↘\\,\\,⌣$ | $\\text{min}$ | $↗\\,\\,⌣$ |\n\nNow, let's sketch our graph: \n\n- We draw a point on the vertical line $x=-1.5$, where the tangent to the graph is horizontal.\n\n- Since $x=-1.5$ is a local minimum, the graph must go up to the left and to the right of that point.\n\n- Finally, the graph must be concave up everywhere.\n\nTherefore, a possible graph of $f$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14254138/assets/8ba702624061a4191ee7d347fe883e8f67d70fab20dca893ddedf1c404305f4b.png)",
